# PlantOps admin console — environment template (Doc 09)
#
# Copy to `apps/admin-web/.env.local` and adjust. Next.js loads `.env*` from
# this directory; the workspace-root `.env` is the API's, validated by
# `libs/config`, and deliberately holds nothing the browser reads.
#
# Everything here is `NEXT_PUBLIC_`, which means Next inlines it into the
# client bundle at build time. That is not a leak, it is the definition: these
# values are as public as the network tab. Nothing secret may be added to this
# file — a secret on a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable is a secret published to every
# visitor.

# The IAM's origin, as the *browser* reaches it. No `/iam` or `/auth` suffix.
#
# The console's dev server runs on 4200 rather than Next's default 3000 so it
# does not collide with the API's own PORT — which is also why the API's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS names http://localhost:4200. In staging and production
# this is the deployed API's URL, and that origin must appear in the API's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS or every request from the console is blocked by the
# browser before it is sent.
NEXT_PUBLIC_IAM_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
